<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="042" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Migrate attachment classification to INVOICE-CLASSIFY@v1</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Swaps one AI call path to an existing pattern (Action + Binding via the 041 facade) and removes its legacy members; behaviour parity is measured, not redesigned.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Literal migration with a reference (agreement-classify Action mirror) and a fixed facade method from 041.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>041</deps>
    <tags>bff, ai, jps, finance</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Move Finance attachment classification from by-name playbook lookup plus C# schema to the Action invoice-classify (spec name INVOICE-CLASSIFY@v1) with its Binding, called through IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync from AttachmentClassificationJobHandler, and remove the classification-only legacy members. Prove the classification results are no worse than before (FR-46).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in JPS Actions, the Binding seed files and the Finance job handlers. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>AttachmentClassificationJobHandler calls IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync; the Action mirror, output-schema mirror and Binding row exist and are seeded in dev; ClassifyAttachmentAsync, ClassificationPlaybookName, FinanceJsonSchemas.ClassificationResultSchema and FinanceOptions.ClassificationDeploymentName are gone; a before / after comparison is recorded.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Today: AttachmentClassificationJobHandler.cs:218 calls IInvoiceAnalysisService.ClassifyAttachmentAsync (IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs:23, InvoiceAnalysisService.cs:63), which loads playbook "FinanceClassification" by name (:35, :74) and calls GetStructuredCompletionAsync with FinanceJsonSchemas.ClassificationResultSchema (FinanceJsonSchemas.cs:9) and FinanceOptions.ClassificationDeploymentName (FinanceOptions.cs:37, default gpt-4o-mini). The handler also consumes InvoiceHints (:301) — keep that type. GetPlaybookByNameAsync and GetStructuredCompletionAsync stay on IInvoiceAi until 050 because extraction still uses them; this task removes only classification-specific members.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/AttachmentClassificationJobHandler.cs (:218 call site; constructor gains IInvoiceAi)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs and InvoiceAnalysisService.cs (remove ClassifyAttachmentAsync and ClassificationPlaybookName)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Models/FinanceJsonSchemas.cs (remove ClassificationResultSchema only)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/FinanceOptions.cs (remove ClassificationDeploymentName) and any appsettings*.json entry for it (shared append point)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/FinanceModule.cs (shared append point; comment at :23; handler registration :156-159)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ConsumerTypes.cs (add InvoiceClassify to All in the same change as the Binding row)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/Adr032/AsymmetricRegistrationTests.cs:59-60 and Adr032/GateCombinationConstructibilityTests.cs:63 (DEF-FIN entries for AttachmentClassificationJobHandler: remove the IInvoiceAnalysisService entry when the handler no longer injects it; a ratchet only shrinks)</file>
      <file role="new">infra/dataverse/actions/invoice-classify.action.json</file>
      <file role="new">infra/dataverse/outputschemas/invoice-classify.schema.json</file>
      <file role="modify">infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json (shared append point: one invoice-classify row)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infra/dataverse/actions/agreement-classify.action.json and infra/dataverse/outputschemas/agreement-classify.schema.json</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Catalog/AgreementClassifyActionContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 (-Filter, -DryRun) and scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1 (-DryRun, -DiffOnly)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Catalog/InvoiceClassifyActionContractTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/finance-intelligence-architecture.md (classification section, lines 41 and 72) and docs/architecture/AI-ARCHITECTURE.md:374 (IInvoiceAi row)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="041" status="required">IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync, its DTOs and ConsumerTypes.InvoiceClassify.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-52 / ADR-039">Prompt and output schema live in the Action row (mirrored in infra/dataverse/); model tier is the Action's (Fast, matching today's gpt-4o-mini) with the Binding's sprk_modeltieroverride. No prompt text, schema or deployment name remains in C# for classification.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039 boot reconciliation">Add ConsumerTypes.InvoiceClassify to ConsumerTypes.All only together with the Binding row; deploy the Binding before (or with) the BFF that lists it, otherwise /healthz reports Unhealthy (RoutingConsumerTypeHealthCheck.cs:251-262).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-46">A missing Binding fails closed with the logged reason code from 041; the handler records the classification as failed (existing failure path) and never falls back to a hard-coded prompt.</constraint>
    <constraint source="repo convention">actionCode is lowercase kebab with no version suffix (invoice-classify); v1 is stated in the description and the JPS version field. The spec's INVOICE-CLASSIFY@v1 is the display name.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not write under .claude/ (jps-action-create Step 5's save under .claude/skills/ is skipped; the mirror under infra/dataverse/actions/ is the saved copy). Keep InvoiceHints, ExtractionResultSchema, ExtractionDeploymentName and GetPlaybookByNameAsync / GetStructuredCompletionAsync (050 removes them).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>JPS Actions and Bindings</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/skills/jps-action-create/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/jps-validate/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-consumer-wiring.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/ai-guide-playbook-deploy-recipe.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/finance-intelligence-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-043-ai-capability-execution-spine.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/jobs.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Action mirror + contract test" location="infra/dataverse/actions/agreement-classify.action.json">Same file shape (systemPrompt, outputSchema, modelTier, temperature, comments); contract test asserts the mirror's schema shape, like AgreementClassifyActionContractTests.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor STANDARD. Read the 041 DTOs, InvoiceAnalysisService.cs:63-116 and the current FinanceClassification playbook text in dev (read-only) so the Action prompt preserves today's instructions.</step>
    <step order="1">Build the before / after set: no classification test set exists in the repo (no InvoiceAnalysisService tests). Take invoices and non-invoices from 001's baseline documents and 002's evaluation set (at least the candidates 001 ran), run today's path in dev and record classification + confidence per document in notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Author the Action with jps-action-create (Fast tier, output schema matching the 041 classify DTO) and validate with jps-validate; write the action and outputschema mirrors and the contract test.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the Binding row; add InvoiceClassify to ConsumerTypes.All.</step>
    <step order="4">Switch AttachmentClassificationJobHandler to IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync, mapping the DTO to the existing hints / confidence handling; remove the classification legacy members listed in the goal and any appsettings entry for ClassificationDeploymentName; update the FinanceModule comment at :23.</step>
    <step order="5">Update handler unit tests (success, missing-Binding fail-closed, Null facade) and the AsymmetricRegistrationTests entry if needed.</step>
    <step order="6">Seed in dev: Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 -Filter invoice-classify -DryRun then live; Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1 -DryRun, live, -DiffOnly (expect no diff). Rerun the before / after set through the new path; record results.</step>
    <step order="7">Update the two architecture docs; build, test, measure publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations (action naming, the before / after set, the seeded row ids) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the after-run classifies any document worse than before (a true invoice no longer InvoiceCandidate, or confidence crossing FinanceOptions.ClassificationConfidenceThreshold the wrong way), STOP and report the comparison before removing the legacy path.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner requires the literal actionCode INVOICE-CLASSIFY@v1 instead of the repo's kebab, no-suffix convention, STOP and ask — the D-64 correction record stores Action code + version, so the choice must be made once for all four Actions.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>FinanceClassification playbook + ClassificationResultSchema + ClassificationDeploymentName do the job today outside the Action spine; no invoice-classify Action or Binding exists (grep infra/dataverse).</existing>
    <extension>The existing playbook cannot be dispatched by IActionRunner (by-name lookup, C# schema); the Action row replaces it rather than adding beside it, and the legacy members are deleted.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-46 and D-52 fail: classification keeps a C# schema and a deployment name in FinanceOptions, and success criterion 12 (one AI path) cannot pass.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 ; scripts/dataverse/Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">infra/dataverse/actions/invoice-classify.action.json, infra/dataverse/outputschemas/invoice-classify.schema.json, infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json</output>
    <output type="code">AttachmentClassificationJobHandler.cs, InvoiceAnalysisService.cs, IInvoiceAnalysisService.cs, FinanceJsonSchemas.cs, FinanceOptions.cs, ConsumerTypes.cs, FinanceModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/contract/Catalog/InvoiceClassifyActionContractTests.cs and updated handler tests</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/ebilling-r1/notes/ before / after classification table</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">AttachmentClassificationJobHandler obtains classification only through IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync; grep finds no ClassifyAttachmentAsync, ClassificationPlaybookName, ClassificationResultSchema or ClassificationDeploymentName in src/ or tests/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The before / after table in notes shows, for every document in the set, the after classification equal to or better than before (FR-46).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with no invoice-classify Binding, the handler logs the reason code ai.invoice.binding_missing, marks the classification failed through its existing failure path and makes no prompt call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the Null facade (AI disabled) the handler follows its existing disabled path without throwing an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Action mirror passes jps-validate; the contract test asserts the output-schema mirror matches the 041 classify DTO fields.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">In dev: the Action row and Binding row exist; Seed-PlaybookConsumers.ps1 -DiffOnly reports no difference; /healthz consumer-type reconciliation is Healthy.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ExtractInvoiceFactsAsync, GetPlaybookByNameAsync, GetStructuredCompletionAsync, ExtractionResultSchema, ExtractionDeploymentName and InvoiceHints still compile and the extraction path tests stay green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-46, D-52. Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs, appsettings*.json, infra/dataverse/sprk_playbookconsumer-rows.json — re-read immediately before editing; add or remove only this task's lines. The brief names scripts/seed-data/Deploy-Actions.ps1; that script seeds the legacy ACT-xxx catalogue, so this task uses the infra/dataverse/actions mirror and scripts/Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 instead (Seed-JpsActions.ps1 is retired, scripts/README.md:171). FR-46 also lists removing GetPlaybookByNameAsync / GetStructuredCompletionAsync and the extraction deployment name: those move to 050 because extraction still calls them until 049 replaces it.

Completed 2026-10-15 (full record: projects/ebilling-r1/notes/042-classify-action-migration.md). Handler now calls IInvoiceAi.ClassifyAsync and fails closed (binding_missing and completion_failed retried while attempts remain then poisoned; output_invalid and the AI kill switch poisoned at once). Legacy classification members removed. Before / after on 35 documents: 0 class changes, 0 regressions, hints equal. Dev: Action row aefb10ba-e0c8-f111-a05c-0022482913fc and Binding row 210fa163-e1c8-f111-a05c-0022482913fc seeded (scripts/ebilling/Ensure-ActionRow.ps1 added because Deploy-ActionMirrors.ps1 cannot create rows). Deviations: the POML's health-check wording was inverted (an All entry without a row is Degraded, a row without an All entry is Unhealthy); Seed-PlaybookConsumers -DiffOnly still shows four pre-existing live-only rows (DEF-016 #1986); dev /healthz/catalog was already 503 (DEF-017 #1987); ClassificationConfidenceThreshold is unused (DEF-018 #1988). Publish size: master 36.44 MB, branch 37.18 MB (Compress-Archive Optimal, linux-x64 framework-dependent, PDBs included, 192 files each); task 042 alone +0.01 MB; no new HIGH CVE. Tests: new seam test 8 and contract test 7 pass; ArchTests 1052 pass (ADR-010 ceiling 162 unchanged); Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests 23382 pass, with 4 to 40 WebApplicationFactory tests timing out at 3 minutes under machine load in each full run, different ones each time and all green when re-run alone. TASK-INDEX.md and current-task.md left for the orchestrator.
rework: none task 042</notes>

  <execution>
